(2) ★ THE DECISIVE TEST, CENTRED.  A first pass that compared lm_q/deg_q directly with
    Gamma^{(q)} failed, and the failure was mine, not the spec's: E5 already showed the
    point prediction carries an O(1e-3) offset at the biased centre, which swamps a
    linear term of the same size.  The estimator must kill constants, so use a CENTRAL
    difference about n_q = round(qT):
        Lhat(h) = [ R(n+) - R(n-) ] / [ lambda(n+) - lambda(n-) ],  n+- = round((q +- hq)T)
    and compare with Phi^{(q)'}(0).  No fitting; h -> 0 is the only extrapolation.
